/// California personal income tax.
///
/// Everyone who `lives us/ca` pays California tax on top of federal tax. This
/// system reads `agi` from the federal tallies (California starts from federal
/// adjusted gross income, the same tally), subtracts the California standard
/// deduction and taxes the rest on the state brackets. Tax withheld or paid to
/// California is credited to the year it is `for`, and what is left is owed by
/// April 15.
///
/// Simplified on purpose: it leaves out itemized deductions, credits, the
/// California differences from federal income (an HSA is taxed here, for one),
/// the state disability insurance payroll tax, the 1% Mental Health Services
/// Tax on taxable income over 1,000,000 USD (R&TC §17043), and the taxing of a
/// part-year resident on only the part of the year (the whole year's income is
/// taxed). Only the `single` and `joint` filing statuses have figures.
///
/// SAMPLE DATA. The figures are community-maintained and were written from the
/// published tables, not checked against the Franchise Tax Board. Verify them
/// against the FTB (ftb.ca.gov, "Tax rate schedules" and "Standard deduction")
/// before relying on them, and correct them in a pull request when they are
/// wrong.
system us/ca

use us
use std


/// The California Franchise Tax Board.
entity ftb : government
  purpose state-tax

/// California income tax withheld from pay, or paid to the FTB directly.
/// Every arrival counts as California tax already paid.


/// Tax withheld from pay, or paid in installments, is credited against the tax
/// owed to California for the year the payment is `for`. It is also a state
/// tax paid, which the federal return itemizes up to a cap.
///
/// To fix: send the payment to a place of kind `ca-tax`, and say what year it is
/// for with `for 2025`.
law credit-ca-payments
  on in
  when to is ftb
  count amount as ca-withheld
  count amount as salt

/// California personal income tax for the year (R&TC §17041), on federal
/// adjusted gross income less the state standard deduction. Long-term gains
/// are taxed as ordinary income here. What was paid by the end of the year is
/// set against it, and the rest is owed by April 15 (Form 540). When more was
/// paid than is due, the amount is negative: a refund.
///
/// To fix: the brackets depend on `filing`: set `filing single` or `filing joint`
/// on the person or household that lives here.
law state-income-tax
  each year closing 04-15
  let taxable = max(value(tally(agi), USD) - deduction[year, owner.filing], empty)
  count taxable as ca-taxable-income
  let liability = progressive(brackets[year, owner.filing], taxable)
  count liability as ca-income-tax
  owe liability - value(tally(ca-withheld), USD) to ftb by date(year + 1, 4, 15) as ca-income-tax

// The marginal rate above each threshold (R&TC §17041), indexed every year.
// The FTB publishes the next year's figures in the autumn; until a row for a
// year is written, the latest earlier row applies, so 2026 uses the 2025
// figures for now.
// verify: the 2025 rows against the FTB's 2025 rate schedules.
param brackets
  2024 single         0 USD 1%    |    10_756 USD 2%    |    25_499 USD 4%    |    40_245 USD 6%    |    55_866 USD 8%    |    70_606 USD 9.3%  |   360_659 USD 10.3% |   432_787 USD 11.3% |   721_314 USD 12.3%
  2024 joint          0 USD 1%    |    21_512 USD 2%    |    50_998 USD 4%    |    80_490 USD 6%    |   111_732 USD 8%    |   141_212 USD 9.3%  |   721_318 USD 10.3% |   865_574 USD 11.3% | 1_442_628 USD 12.3%
  2025 single         0 USD 1%    |    11_079 USD 2%    |    26_264 USD 4%    |    41_452 USD 6%    |    57_542 USD 8%    |    72_724 USD 9.3%  |   371_479 USD 10.3% |   445_771 USD 11.3% |   742_953 USD 12.3%
  2025 joint          0 USD 1%    |    22_158 USD 2%    |    52_528 USD 4%    |    82_904 USD 6%    |   115_084 USD 8%    |   145_448 USD 9.3%  |   742_958 USD 10.3% |   891_542 USD 11.3% | 1_485_906 USD 12.3%

// The California standard deduction (R&TC §17073.5).
// verify: the 2025 figures against the FTB.
param deduction
  2024 single  5_540 USD
  2024 joint  11_080 USD
  2025 single  5_706 USD
  2025 joint  11_412 USD
